<main class="faq-main">
    <div class="faq-intro">
        <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
        <p>Answers to the questions we hear most often.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
        <h2>The bottom player bar or Queue button is cut off or hard to tap on my phone</h2>
        <p>
            On some phones the player bar can feel cramped. A couple of quick fixes usually
            help right away:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Zoom out a little - use pinch-to-zoom, or your browser's page zoom / text size
                setting - to give the bar more room to breathe.</li>
            <li>Tap the fullscreen icon in the room header to hide your browser's toolbar and
                give the player more space to work with.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We're actively working on making the player bar fit better on every screen size.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
        <h2>How do I install this as an app on my iPhone?</h2>
        <p>You can add EndAuxRacism to your Home Screen so it opens like a regular app:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Open this site in Safari (this only works in Safari, not Chrome or other
                iPhone browsers).</li>
            <li>Tap the Share button in the toolbar (the square with an arrow pointing up).</li>
            <li>Scroll down and tap <strong>Add to Home Screen</strong>.</li>
            <li>Tap <strong>Add</strong> in the top right.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
            Once it's added, tapping the icon on your Home Screen opens the app in fullscreen,
            without the browser's address bar - just like a native app.
        </p>
        <p class="faq-note">
            <strong>Note for Android users:</strong> adding this site to your home screen from
            Chrome or Firefox currently opens it as a normal browser tab rather than
            fullscreen. This is a known limitation of how the app is set up right now, not a
            problem with your phone or browser.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-item">
        <h2>Playback stops when my phone's screen turns off (Android)</h2>
        <p>
            This is usually caused by your phone's battery-saving settings, which can
            restrict background audio for browser apps once the screen turns off. To fix it:
        </p>
        <ol>
            <li>Open your phone's Settings app.</li>
            <li>Find your browser app (Chrome, Firefox, etc.) under Apps or App info.</li>
            <li>Look for Permissions, and make sure "Music and audio" (or a similar
                background playback permission) is turned on.</li>
            <li>Also look for battery options like "Pause app activity if unused" or "Manage
                app if unused," and turn those off for your browser app.</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="faq-note">
            This is a setting controlled by your phone's operating system, not something the
            app itself can turn on from the browser.
        </p>
    </div>
</main>

</body>
